Imou IPC-C22E-S2-v2: make the microSD slot work.

On this board the SD power switch on PAD_FUART_RTS is active-high (the
SigmaStar reference design the driver follows is active-low), and the SD
pads need their input buffers enabled the way the stock U-Boot does.
Board-specific, so it is carried by this device rather than the shared
infinity6b0 kernel. Reverse-engineered and tested on hardware by
ABATAPA in OpenIPC/builder#39.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6b0.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6b0.dtsi
index 946e1fc..d77514b 100755
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6b0.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6b0.dtsi
@@ -597,7 +597,7 @@
 
             slot-ip-orders = <0>,<1>,<2>; // 0:IP_SD 1:IP_SDIO
             slot-pad-orders = <0>,<1>,<2>; // 0:PAD_SD 1:PAD_SD1
-            slot-max-clks = <48000000>,<48000000>,<48000000>;
+            slot-max-clks = <43200000>,<43200000>,<43200000>;
             slot-intcdzs = <1>,<1>,<1>;
             slot-fakecdzs = <0>,<0>,<0>;
             slot-cdzs-gpios = <PAD_PM_SD_CDZ>,<PAD_SD1_IO6>,<0>;
